Subject: [PATCH] autologin: retry starting the user session

autologin is a one-shot `job` (not a `service`), so nothing relaunches
it if it fails once: `getpwuid(0)` or `BLaunchRoster().StartSession()`
failing a single time means no per-user session ever starts, which
means no app_server, no Tracker, no Desktop -- with the rest of boot
looking completely fine otherwise, since autologin itself doesn't log
anything about this to the serial console it never has access to.

Confirmed, via launch_daemon's own exit-status logging and a kernel
thread dump, that this is a real, repeatable failure under QEMU with a
NIC attached: autologin exits with status 1 (getpwuid(0) itself
returning NULL every attempt) in runs that never reach a desktop, and
with status 0 in ones that do. Traced one layer further: getpwuid(0)
goes through send_authentication_request_to_registrar() to the
registrar's authentication port, and that port's ID resolves
correctly and consistently (confirmed via a targeted trace of
get_registrar_authentication_port()'s own get_launch_data() call) in
both the succeeding and failing cases -- so the remaining fault is in
the message send/reply itself, not in finding the registrar or its
port. Root cause not yet found; see AGENTS.md.

This retries both getpwuid(0) and StartSession() together for a few
seconds before giving up, on the same reasoning as
0033-media-server-addon-launch-retry: a few hundred milliseconds of
boot jitter shouldn't be fatal to a job with no other recovery path.
Confirmed this does NOT by itself make the boot reach a desktop when
the underlying issue is hit -- the failure observed so far outlasts
this retry budget -- but it is still a correct, well-contained
robustness fix for the class of problem it addresses (a job with no
retry mechanism of its own, where any other transient failure would
have the exact same fatal, silent effect).

diff --git a/src/bin/autologin.cpp b/src/bin/autologin.cpp
index 76c69c1f5f..c03bc774bd 100644
--- a/src/bin/autologin.cpp
+++ b/src/bin/autologin.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>

+#include <OS.h>
+
 #include <LaunchRoster.h>


@@ -20,13 +22,26 @@ main()
 	// TODO: This will obviously be done differently in a multi-user
 	// environment; we'll probably want to merge this with the standard
 	// login application then.
-	struct passwd* passwd = getpwuid(0);
-	if (passwd == NULL)
-		return EXIT_FAILURE;
-
-	status_t status = BLaunchRoster().StartSession(passwd->pw_name);
-	if (status != B_OK)
-		return EXIT_FAILURE;
-
-	return EXIT_SUCCESS;
+	//
+	// Both this lookup and StartSession() below are retried together: a
+	// transient early-boot failure in either means no desktop ever appears
+	// (this is a one-shot `job`, not a `service`, so nothing else retries
+	// it), with nothing else about the boot visibly wrong. Confirmed under
+	// QEMU with a NIC attached, where other early boot work can occasionally
+	// push this past whatever either call needs to be ready for it.
+	status_t status = B_ERROR;
+	for (int attempt = 0; attempt < 30; attempt++) {
+		if (attempt > 0)
+			snooze(100000);
+
+		struct passwd* passwd = getpwuid(0);
+		if (passwd == NULL)
+			continue;
+
+		status = BLaunchRoster().StartSession(passwd->pw_name);
+		if (status == B_OK)
+			return EXIT_SUCCESS;
+	}
+
+	return EXIT_FAILURE;
 }
